<title>CANADA: AlphaStar allowed use of U.S. satellite.</title>
<headline>AlphaStar allowed use of U.S. satellite.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's industry minister said on Thursday that AlphaStar Canada Inc, a subsidiary of Tee-Comm Electronics Inc, has been authorized for an interim period to use U.S. fixed satellite capacity to provide direct-to-home broadcast (DTH) services in Canada.</p>
<p>Industry Minister John Manley said a key condition of the uplink license is AlphaStar's commitment to transfer its Canadian direct-to-home services to Canadian fixed satellite facilities when suitable capacity becomes available.</p>
</text>
